      "previewImage": "previews/minimax-h3-10eros-turbo-t2v.jpg",
      "description": "The 10Eros Max finetune paired with the v4-600 EMA Turbo LoRA at 6 steps.\n\nThe Turbo LoRA composes cleanly with this non-pruned base. Its adaln update lives in the 2688-dim silu(t_emb) space and is re-injected at runtime on to the adaln projection's OUTPUT (96768 wide on both the stock pruned base and this one), so the differing input compression is not involved. Verified in practice, not just on paper — the node reports the LoRA active with 47 patches attached and a clean RMS trajectory.\n\nMeasured 70.7s at 5s/480p/6 steps on a 12 GB RTX 4070 Ti with the app's accelerator toggles on.\n\nNote: on long, detail-heavy prompts the accelerator toggles cost more time than they save on this hardware. If a 15s character-and-dialogue prompt runs slower than you expect, try turning Spectrum and Sol-Attn off — output is indistinguishable and it measured roughly twice as fast without them.",
